I restructured the checks to return early for the uncommon valid-type case and added branch-prediction hints so the common lazy-resolution path is fall-through, reducing taken branches.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 0)) {
        return type;
    }
    if (__builtin_expect(profile != NULL && profileIndex < profile->numFields, 1)) {
        return profile->fields[profileIndex].type;
    }
    return type;
}
```